1. Definitions

"Stasis" means the software and associated materials in this repository, including
the compiler, runtime, standard library, tools, samples, and documentation, but
excluding any subdirectory that contains its own LICENSE file.

"Licensee" means (a) a company or other legal entity that uses Stasis, or (b) if
no such entity applies, the individual person using Stasis.

"Gross Revenue" means the total gross revenue of the Licensee for a given
calendar year (January 1 through December 31) that is directly attributable to
the Distribution of artifacts built using Stasis, before expenses. Revenue from
products not built using Stasis is excluded.

"Distribute" (or "Distribution") means to provide, publish, ship, deploy, or
otherwise make available to any third party any binary, executable, application,
game, or other artifact built using Stasis (including alpha, beta, and tester
builds), whether for free or for a fee.

"Internal Use" means use of Stasis entirely within the Licensee's organization,
without any Distribution.

